## edge cases

### [setup] deep folder tree for recursive move verification
POST http://localhost:8080/api/directory?path=tree/

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/directory?path=tree/level1/

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/directory?path=tree/level1/level2/

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource?path=tree/level1/level2/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="leaf.txt"

< ../src/test/resources/test-files/TZ.md
--boundary--

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/directory?path=dest/

### move folder with deep nested structure - 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource/move?from=tree/&to=dest/tree/

### verify nested file is reachable at NEW location - 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/resource?path=dest/tree/level1/level2/leaf.txt

### verify OLD root folder no longer exists — 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/resource?path=tree/

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/directory?path=empty-dir/

### move an empty folder (no content, removeObjects called with empty list) — 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource/move?from=empty-dir/&to=empty-dir-renamed/

### move with double slash in path — 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource/move?from=archive//data.txt&to=archive/data_v3.txt

### move-then-move-back (idempotency round-trip) — 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/directory?path=ping/

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource/move?from=ping/&to=pong/

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource/move?from=pong/&to=ping/

### URL-encoded space in target name — 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource/move?from=note.txt&to=my%20note.txt

### attempt to access another user's resource — 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/resource/move?from=user-3-files/secret.txt&to=stolen.txt